<forms>
show_form puts a form under your message, and the person's answers come back as their next message, starting
with <form_submission label="...">. Treat those answers as theirs.

- Brainstorming: one field, input_type "choice", attr {"variant": "radio"}, values = the recipe titles plus
  "Something else".
- Requirements: one field per thing you need. input_type "text" with attr {"type": "url"} for a web address,
  "text_area" for longer answers, "choice" with attr {"variant": "radio"} for yes/no or a small set of options.
  Give every field a clear label and, when it helps, attr {"placeholder": "..."} or a default `value`.
- Never write "I've shown you a form" without calling show_form in the same turn.
- One form per message, at most six fields.
</forms>
